{"format_version":1,"partition":19403,"records":{"bibbern":{"entries":[["bibbern",null,"[ˈbɪbɐn]","The contemporary form since the 19th century from Low German bibbern, probably already Middle Low German *bibberen, a frequentative of bēven (from Old Saxon bibōn, bivon), from Proto-West Germanic *bibēn, cognate of modern German beben.\nCompare Dutch bibberen (1700), English biver. In spite of the late attestations, these informal verbs might be rather old in view of the etymologically regular gemination -ēv- → -ibb-, though this can also be due to analogy. Earlier High German variants are bebern, bebbern (18th c.), perhaps also pöpern (East Central German, late 17th c.). These are formed directly from beben.",null,"haben"]],"senses":[[418765,"bibbern","verb","to shiver",0],[418766,"bibbern","verb","to jitter",1]],"related_forms":[[57459,"bibbern","bibbern","derived"],[57460,"bibbern","schütteln","related"],[57461,"bibbern","beben","related"],[57462,"bibbern","frösteln","related"],[57463,"bibbern","frieren","related"]]},"dickbäuchigeren":{"entries":[["dickbäuchigeren",null,null,null]],"senses":[[462336,"dickbäuchigeren","adj","inflection of dickbäuchig:",0],[462337,"dickbäuchigeren","adj","strong genitive masculine/neuter singular comparative degree",1],[462338,"dickbäuchigeren","adj","weak/mixed genitive/dative all-gender singular comparative degree",2],[462339,"dickbäuchigeren","adj","strong/weak/mixed accusative masculine singular comparative degree",3],[462340,"dickbäuchigeren","adj","strong dative plural comparative degree",4],[462341,"dickbäuchigeren","adj","weak/mixed all-case plural comparative degree",5]],"inflections":[["dickbäuchigeren","dickbäuchig","comparative,genitive,masculine,singular,strong,without-article"]]},"fändet statt":{"entries":[["fändet statt",null,null,null]],"senses":[[275484,"fändet statt","verb","second-person plural subjunctive II of stattfinden",0]]},"stornierung":{"entries":[["stornierung",null,null,"stornieren + -ung, from Italian st